{"id": "EUVD-2026-80434", "enisaUuid": "d4d4cc95-8d75-3f4e-805e-7c9b3b19e119", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nf2fs: fix to migrate all curseg types during free_segment_range\n\nIn free_segment_range(), the curseg evacuation loop only iterates up to\nNR_CURSEG_PERSIST_TYPE (0..5), missing non-persistent in-memory curseg\ntypes such as CURSEG_COLD_DATA_PINNED and CURSEG_ALL_DATA_ATGC.\n\nEven though these in-memory curseg types are not saved in the on-disk\ncheckpoint header, they still occupy active physical segments at runtime.\nIf an active in-memory curseg happens to be allocated within the segment\nrange being truncated during filesystem shrink, failing to evacuate it\nwill cause subsequent writes to the curseg attempting out-of-bounds I/O\non the truncated storage range.\n\nFix this by expanding the curseg evacuation loop upper bound to\nNR_CURSEG_TYPE to ensure all active curseg types are safely migrated\nout of the target range.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:31:07", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:48:57", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d358d2fc6be11eefde5eb1286f1c43a6d0330db6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3b85edf3391f3e1f624f409a7d2d239885f567b7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b8ae1228c153622afa71a179c9d4dc268117e0f0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b9776094aa7118e8e5dfdcd791ffc8330c5ca408", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8ec06f50ddd8d201bd7e55b896ae28ed9d4cb7d1"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89834", "GHSA-92fw-gww6-96g8"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00cae18c-d4e3-3e15-a7d4-6b792eb6086f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d0b9e42ab6155dc05fc83f00af9f45d4dd02264d <b8ae1228c153622afa71a179c9d4dc268117e0f0"}, {"id": "449a26d2-54f5-31ca-8b35-85dfb8a8cd67", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "48bba8fc-ec77-3b77-9253-8e14e5725909", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d0b9e42ab6155dc05fc83f00af9f45d4dd02264d <3b85edf3391f3e1f624f409a7d2d239885f567b7"}, {"id": "76ec8ec3-7bad-3b1e-a0e0-564dab2a8c86", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "80e8c43d-c417-3c54-a8c7-24cdb71f7108", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10"}, {"id": "85f9aa60-93a9-3301-824d-edab349140b7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "899c36b3-e624-3479-af78-2066d3ae2c26", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d0b9e42ab6155dc05fc83f00af9f45d4dd02264d <d358d2fc6be11eefde5eb1286f1c43a6d0330db6"}, {"id": "93097e2c-ef93-346d-8f53-4f12afe1b985", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "c9aee7ca-ba3e-3532-bc4e-60cdda8fa68f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d0b9e42ab6155dc05fc83f00af9f45d4dd02264d <b9776094aa7118e8e5dfdcd791ffc8330c5ca408"}, {"id": "cf3a5e8c-6f7c-34fc-9d3b-ae6c38b3471b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "d0ea4d63-47db-3411-8f16-7855860bfd1c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "fbe67199-79c2-3264-9a9a-2b1669a014ea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d0b9e42ab6155dc05fc83f00af9f45d4dd02264d <8ec06f50ddd8d201bd7e55b896ae28ed9d4cb7d1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "58ae033c-6d31-3b15-ad29-ff25cb47c459", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}